NEARS-1610 — PRE-EXISTING (not introduced by this change)
Cold category cache => the interest screen never opens at all.

Repro (live, emulator-5556, network HEALTHY):
 1. Change app language (Settings > Language) -> LocalClient.clearCache() wipes the cache.
    VERIFIED at storage layer: sqlite cache_response rows LIKE '/api/v1/categories%' == 0
 2. Select module "Food & Restaurant" (module 2), network UP, user emily.johnson@demo.com
    (module_ids did not yet contain 2, so shouldShowInterestPage() == true).
 OBSERVED: app routed straight to module-2 HOME. Interest screen never appeared.
 3. Immediately after, sqlite shows '/api/v1/categories 2' now PRESENT
    -> the network fetch DID run, but completed AFTER the navigation gate had already decided.
 4. Re-select the SAME module (cache now warm) -> interest screen opens normally (10 cards).

Mechanism (pre-existing, unchanged by NEARS-1610):
  CategoryController.getCategoryList(local) awaits ONLY the cache read, then fires the
  network leg WITHOUT await. ModuleController._showInterestPage()'s .then() therefore
  evaluates `categoryList != null` while the network call is still in flight; on a cold
  cache it is null, so the else-branch Get.offAllNamed(initialRoute) sends the user home.
  The identical unawaited-recall shape exists on the base commit, so this predates the ticket.

Consequence for AC2: the screen can only be ENTERED when categoryList is already non-null,
but _categoryFetchFailed can only be raised when _categoryList IS null -> the NearsErrorRetry
surface is not reachable by user navigation on mobile.
